ear":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":1758000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":20864,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":24524,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2465.98,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":276.46,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":null,"documents":[],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-12","committee":"Communities and Wellbeing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Special Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-18","committee":"Special Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-30","committee":"Communities and Wellbeing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-04","committee":"Special Scrutiny Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-05","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Hyndburn removed Cabinet from audit committee but has not appointed replacements","lead":"The council agreed in June 2024 to strengthen the independence of its Audit Committee\u2014which provides the council's independent check on spending and decision-making\u2014by removing Cabinet members, in compliance with professional guidance. However, the planned appointment of two independent members to fill those seats has not progressed. The council states that the delay reflects \"numerous complex corporate priorities, plus Local Government Reorganisation preparations\" that have prevented senior officials from advancing the work. The paper presented to this month's Audit Committee meeting indicates the process remains incomplete and provides no timeframe for completing the appointments.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Appointment of Independent Members to Audit Committee Position Update Sept 2026","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24324/24324.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Hyndburn council faces \u00a3845,000 four-year funding gap for local plan delivery","lead":"Hyndburn council has identified a \u00a3844,800 shortfall over four years to fund its local plan \u2014 the blueprint for where homes and businesses can be built \u2014 after government grant funding ends next year. The council is spending an estimated \u00a3970,000 to produce the plan, covering staff, environmental assessments and public consultation, but has only \u00a3125,200 available. A one-off government grant of \u00a3108,000 runs until 2026/27; after that, the council's regular budget of \u00a34,300 a year will fall far short of the estimated \u00a395,000 to \u00a3475,000 needed annually. In the 2027/28 financial year alone, the council faces a shortfall of \u00a3470,700. The council has flagged the gap in its budget papers but has not yet committed additional funding. Internal audit opinion improved slightly in 2025/26, though a payroll system audit received limited assurance, indicating some control weaknesses.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Preliminary Local Plan Budget","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24350/24350.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Appointment of Independent Members to Audit Committee Position Update Sept 2026","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24324/24324.pdf","headline":"The council improved audit independence by removing Cabinet members from the Audit Committee, but the appointment of independent members has not progressed in over two years due to competing corporate priorities and reorganisation preparations.","detail":"In June 2024, the Council agreed to appoint two independent persons to the Audit Committee. Cabinet members were subsequently removed to ensure the Committee's independence and compliance with CIPFA guidance. However, the appointment process has not advanced. The paper states that the next step of reporting to Leaders Policy Board has been delayed because \"numerous complex corporate priorities, plus Local Government Reorganisation preparations have meant that the Executive Director (Legal & Democratic Services) has not been able to progress this further.\"","category":"governance","matters":"Lenders care about whether a council's audit function is independent and well-governed. While removing Cabinet members strengthens governance, the multi-year delay and stated reason\u2014competing priorities and reorganisation distractions\u2014could signal resource constraints or misaligned priorities within council leadership.","figures":"Agreement made June 2024; update provided September 2026, with appointments process still incomplete after two years","quote":"Cabinet members were removed from the Committee to ensure its independence and compliance with CIPFA guidance.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"(c) Audit Committee Minutes - 29 June 2026","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24317/24317.pdf","headline":"Payroll system audit received limited assurance, identifying control weaknesses despite no material impact","detail":"The payroll system audit received 'Limited Assurance' in 2025/26, indicating identified control weaknesses in this critical financial function. Of 14 audit reports issued, 13 received comprehensive or substantial assurance, with payroll being the sole limited assurance rating. The council notes this did not materially affect the financial statements.","category":"audit","matters":"Payroll is a critical control; lenders need visibility of control weaknesses even if immaterial to financial reporting, and need to see evidence the council is addressing them","figures":"13 of 14 audits at comprehensive/substantial assurance (7 comprehensive, 6 substantial, 1 limited, 0 no assurance)","quote":"The audit engagement was the Payroll System. Whilst this was given 'Limited Assurance,' this did not have any material effect on the Council's Financial Statements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"(c) Audit Committee Minutes - 29 June 2026","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24317/24317.pdf","headline":"Internal audit opinion improved, with score moving from 1.53 to 1.47 in 2025/26","detail":"The Head of Audit issued a positive opinion on the council's internal controls based on 2025/26 work. The opinion score improved from 1.53 in 2024/25 to 1.47 in 2025/26, indicating strengthened control effectiveness. Audit plan coverage reached 95.96%, 2.04% below the 98% target but 5.53% higher than the prior year.","category":"audit","matters":"Improving audit opinion signals strengthening financial controls, which reduces lending risk and gives lenders confidence in council governance","figures":"Opinion score 1.53 (2024/25) to 1.47 (2025/26); audit coverage 95.96% vs 98% target and 89.43% prior year","quote":"The Head of Audit & Investigations issued a positive opinion on the systems of Internal Control based on the work carried out in 2025/26. The opinion score slightly improved from 1.53 in 2024/25 to 1.47 in 2025/26.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Appendix 2 - Preliminary Local Plan Budget","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24350/24350.pdf","headline":"The council has identified an \u00a3844,800 four-year funding shortfall for local plan delivery, with grant funding ending after 2026/27 but costs continuing at \u00a395,000-\u00a3475,000 per year.","detail":"The budget estimates total costs of \u00a3970,000 for local plan production (staffing, environmental assessments, heritage assessments, consultations, examination) against available budget of \u00a3125,200. This includes a one-off grant of \u00a3108,000 in 2026/27; the council's regular local plan budget is \u00a34,300/year. The funding gap becomes acute when grant funding ends: 2027/28 shows estimated spend of \u00a3475,000 against a budget of \u00a34,300, creating a single-year shortfall of \u00a3470,700. The document explicitly identifies this as 'Additional Budget Required'.","category":"governance","matters":"The local plan is a statutory requirement. A lender needs to understand whether the council can meet this duty and how it will fund the identified shortfall\u2014whether from reserves, borrowing, or by scaling back work.","figures":"Total estimated spend \u00a3970,000; total available budget \u00a3125,200; total four-year shortfall \u00a3844,800. In 2027/28 alone: spend \u00a3475,000 against budget \u00a34,300.","quote":"Additional Budget Required \u00a3470,700.00","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-05","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"PIs Monitoring and TM strategy Q1 2026/27 - Main Report","paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24142/24142.pdf","headline":"The council is planning to draw down useable reserves over the MTFS period to support the revenue budget","detail":"The Liability Benchmark revision explicitly includes 'the increased draw down of useable reserves anticipated to support the revenue budget over the MTFS period.' This indicates the council cannot balance current revenue spending from income and is relying on reserve depletion.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve drawdown to fund revenue is a sign of structural deficit; finite reserves depleting annually will eventually create a financial cliff unless underlying spending or income patterns change, creating risk for creditors.","figures":"Drawdown amount not quantified in this report","quote":"The inputs that determine the Liability Benchmark have been revised to include the increased capital expenditure relating to vehicle leasing and the increased draw down of useable reserves anticipated to support the revenue budget over the MTFS period.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Hyndburn BC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Payroll system audit received limited assurance, identifying control weaknesses despite no material impact","lead":"Payroll is a critical control; lenders need visibility of control weaknesses even if immaterial to financial reporting, and need to see evidence the council is addressing them","also":["2 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Communities and Wellbeing Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-10-12","n_findings":3,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"(c) Audit Committee Minutes - 29 June 2026","top_paper_url":"http://democracy.hyndburnbc.gov.uk/documents/s24317/24317.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":58,"news_drafts_total":2}}